---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { formatDate, getPosts, postUrl } from '../site';

const posts = await getPosts();
---

<Base>
  <section class="intro prose">
    <h1>Infrastructure engineer. Evidence first, everything as code.</h1>
    <p>
      I've spent a decade building and running cloud platforms, from industrial IoT fleets to e-learning platforms
      on Kubernetes. I debug production-scale problems from the evidence up, turn the fix into code and runbooks,
      and build guardrails so AI agents can work safely on real infrastructure.
    </p>
    <ul class="highlights">
      <li>
        <strong>200/200</strong> concurrent users on a JupyterHub platform, up from 15–23% failed logins, after
        tracing the cause to load-balancer churn from node autoscaling
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>900+ lifts</strong> monitored in production by Franz, an IoT platform whose team I led from zero to
        MVP in under six months
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Default-deny</strong> tool access for a Claude Code pipeline that reads untrusted tickets, with
        humans approving every merge
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Senior DevOps/Infrastructure Engineer at Multiverse, previously Tech Lead at Relayr. More in
      <a href="/work/">My Work</a> and <a href="/about/">About</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2 class="section-title">Writing</h2>
  <ol class="post-list">
    {
      posts.map((post) => (
        <li>
          <article>
            <h3>
              <a href={postUrl(post)}>{post.data.title}</a>
            </h3>
            <time class="post-date" datetime={post.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>
              {formatDate(post.data.date)}
            </time>
            {post.data.description && <p>{post.data.description}</p>}
          </article>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
</Base>
